  "meta": {
    "document": "City and County of Denver FY2026 Adopted Budget",
    "title": "Denver — the money trail",
    "grand_total": 4435670537,
    "year": 2026,
    "note": "Denver is a consolidated city-and-county — one government, one budget, no separate county line (the Assessor, Sheriff, and Clerk are city departments). This is the adopted all-funds budget for 2026, $4.44 billion. The General Fund is $1.68 billion; the biggest non-General-Fund pieces are self-supporting enterprises — Denver International Airport ($789M in operations) and Wastewater. The total is shown net of about $447M in interfund transfers, so those dollars aren’t counted twice. Every figure ties to Denver’s 2026 Final Budget Book and foots to the dollar."
  },
